{
 "title": "Muni vehicle type by route (weekday) and Metro train length, with SFMTA vehicle capacity standards",
 "accessed": "2026-10-05",
 "rawDir": "data/beta3/raw/fleet/",
 "sources": [
  {
   "id": "calitp_vl_2026-06-10",
   "publisher": "Cal-ITP (California Integrated Travel Project), public GCS bucket calitp-publish-data-analysis (UC Davis transit priority 2026 extract)",
   "url": "https://storage.googleapis.com/calitp-publish-data-analysis/ucd_transit_priority_2026/fct_vehicle_locations_2026-06-10/fct_vehicle_locations_2026-06-10_000000000000.jsonl.gz",
   "urlPattern": "…/fct_vehicle_locations_2026-06-10/fct_vehicle_locations_2026-06-10_{000000000000..000000000399}.jsonl.gz (400 shards, 2.83 GB, statewide)",
   "date": "2026-06-10 (Wed). The dt partition is a UTC day, so it covers 17:00 PDT Tue 2026-06-09 to 17:00 PDT Wed 2026-06-10. AM peak and midday come from Wed; PM peak and evening come from Tue. Both are weekdays.",
   "rawFile": "muni_vl_2026-06-10.jsonl.gz (1,533,895 Muni rows; fields hour, vehicle_id, vehicle_label, trip_id, trip_route_id, direction, occupancy, location_timestamp)",
   "method": "Streamed every shard and kept gtfs_dataset_name = 'Bay Area 511 Muni VehiclePositions'. Each (service day, trip_id) is treated as a trip, and each vehicle seen on it in at least 3 distinct minutes counts as one trip-vehicle assignment. The vehicle type comes from the fleet number range (vehicleNumberRanges). Shares are trip-weighted, over the whole day and over the peak (trip median time 06:00-09:00 or 16:00-19:00 PT). weekdayVehicle is the length class if it covers 90% or more of bus assignments, otherwise 'mixed'. trolley is true if trolley coaches cover 50% or more of assignments. The feed carries one vehicle_id per train, so it cannot show consist length."
  },
  {
   "id": "sfmta_srtp_fy19-30",
   "publisher": "SFMTA",
   "title": "Short Range Transit Plan FY2019-FY2030 (SFMTA Board 2019-12-03, Item 15)",
   "url": "https://www.sfmta.com/sites/default/files/reports-and-documents/2019/11/12-3-19_item_15_short_range_transit_plan_fy19-30.pdf",
   "date": "2019-12-03",
   "rawFile": "data/beta3/raw/params/sfmta_SRTP_FY19-30.pdf (+ .txt), already in repo raw",
   "method": "Table 4-5, Passenger Load Standards - Rail (from the 2019 Rail Fleet Management Plan). Table 4-6, Passenger Load Standards - Bus (from the 2017 Bus FMP). Table 6-8, Fleet Inventory, with fleet ID ranges and crowding capacity by type. Chapter 2 division/yard table (vehicle counts by yard)."
  },
  {
   "id": "sfmta_bus_fmp_2017",
   "publisher": "SFMTA (hosted by SF Controller, Muni Reliability Working Group)",
   "title": "SFMTA Bus Fleet Management Plan 2017-2030",
   "url": "https://sfcontroller.org/sites/default/files/Muni%20Reliability%20Working%20Group/2017%20Bus%20Fleet%20Plan.pdf",
   "date": "2017",
   "rawFile": "bus_fmp_2017.pdf (+ .txt)",
   "method": "Table 2: Average Maximum and Crowding Loads by bus length (4.5 and 3.0 sq ft per standee). Footnote: crush load is 1.5 sq ft per passenger (APTA gross load)."
  },
  {
   "id": "sfmta_mewg_2024-09-19",
   "publisher": "SFMTA",
   "title": "Muni Equity Working Group, 2024-09-19 slides (p.31, capacity thresholds)",
   "url": "https://www.sfmta.com/media/40553/download",
   "date": "2024-09-19",
   "rawFile": "data/beta3/raw/reliability/muni_equity_wg_2024-09-19.pdf (+ .txt), already in repo raw",
   "method": "Three capacity thresholds. Planning: 4.5 sq ft per standee (bus), 3.7 (rail). Crowding: 3.0 (bus), 2.7 (rail). Crush: 1.5 (bus), 1.8 (rail). Worked example for a 40 ft motor coach: planning 44, crowding 51, crush 71."
  },
  {
   "id": "sfmta_mses_2026",
   "publisher": "SFMTA",
   "title": "Muni Service Equity Strategy FY26-27 & FY27-28 (Board 2026-04-07)",
   "url": "https://www.sfmta.com/media/44786/download?inline",
   "date": "2026-04-07",
   "rawFile": "data/beta3/raw/reliability/mse_report_fy27-28_2026-04-07.pdf (+ .txt), already in repo raw",
   "method": "Crowding definition: a stop is crowded when the load is at or above the vehicle's crowding capacity, and a trip is crowded when 5% or more of its stops are. Figure 7 lists the K Ingleside Rapid Project with 2-car trains on Ocean Ave as partly done and partly in progress."
  },
  {
   "id": "sfmta_svc_2025-02-01",
   "publisher": "SFMTA",
   "title": "Muni Service Changes: February 1, 2025",
   "url": "https://www.sfmta.com/travel-updates/muni-service-changes-february-1-2025",
   "date": "2025-01 (effective 2025-02-01)",
   "rawFile": "muni-service-changes-february-1-2025.html",
   "method": "States that the K Ingleside and M Ocean View lines will run one-car trains on weekends, which implies two-car trains on weekdays."
  },
  {
   "id": "sfmta_svc_2025-02-01_detail",
   "publisher": "SFMTA",
   "title": "Muni Service Changes: Effective Saturday, February 1, 2025 (K/L/M detail)",
   "url": "https://www.sfmta.com/travel-updates/muni-service-changes-effective-saturday-february-1-2025",
   "date": "2025-01",
   "rawFile": "muni-service-changes-effective-saturday-february-1-2025.html",
   "method": "States that the K Ingleside will operate two-car trains westbound as far as the City College pedestrian bridge, where the second car is taken out of service."
  },
  {
   "id": "sfmta_blog_k_return_2021",
   "publisher": "SFMTA",
   "title": "Welcome Back to the Westside, K Ingleside Trains! (2021-04-16)",
   "url": "https://www.sfmta.com/blog/welcome-back-westside-k-ingleside-trains",
   "date": "2021-04-16",
   "rawFile": "welcome-back-westside-k-ingleside-trains.html",
   "method": "Says 'the two-car train increases the N Judah's capacity'."
  },
  {
   "id": "sfmta_blog_two_car_2018",
   "publisher": "SFMTA",
   "title": "Two Car Trains On The Move (2018-06-05)",
   "url": "https://www.sfmta.com/blog/two-car-trains-move",
   "date": "2018-06-05",
   "rawFile": "two-car-trains-move.html",
   "method": "First LRV4 two-car trains, on the N Judah."
  },
  {
   "id": "wiki_muni_fleet",
   "publisher": "Wikipedia, San Francisco Municipal Railway fleet (cites SFMTA and the trade press)",
   "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco_Municipal_Railway_fleet",
   "date": "accessed 2026-10-05",
   "rawFile": "wiki_muni_fleet.html (+ .txt)",
   "method": "Current fleet number series by model and yard, including the ENC 32-ft 8531-8560 (2021), XT40 5701-5885, and battery test buses 5001-5012. Also: 'only around 130 LRVs are scheduled for service during rush hour', citing Tramways & Urban Transit (Dec 2025) and Passenger Train Journal (Nov 2025), neither available online."
  },
  {
   "id": "wiki_metro_lines",
   "publisher": "Wikipedia, J Church / N Judah / K Ingleside / T Third Street articles",
   "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J_Church",
   "date": "accessed 2026-10-05",
   "rawFile": "J_Church.html, N_Judah.html, K_Ingleside.html, T_Third_Street.html, L_Taraval.html, M_Ocean_View.html, S_Shuttle.html",
   "method": "J: 'almost always run with a single car' because stops in the right-of-way are too short. N: 'largely uses two-car (150-foot) trains'. K/T: permanent two-car trains since 2018-08-25 (SFMTA press release, cited)."
  },
  {
   "id": "sfmta_zeb_rollout_2022",
   "publisher": "SFMTA",
   "title": "Zero-Emission Bus Rollout Plan (2022)",
